  <div class="lh-container">

<div class="bt">Likutay Halachos — Orach Chaim, Volume 2</div>
<div class="ht">Hilchos Tefilas HaMinchah [Laws of the Afternoon Prayer]<br>Halachah 4 (§§ 1–14)<br><span style="font-size:.95rem;font-weight:400">Based on <span class="lr">LM I:64</span> (<i>Bo El Pharaoh</i>)</span></div>

<div class="sn">Introduction — The <i>Chalal HaPanui</i>, <i>Emunah</i>, and <i>Tefilas HaMinchah</i></div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Halachah</span>: Our Sages warned especially about <span class="h">Tefilas HaMinchah</span>: <span class="mx">"one should always be careful with <i>Tefilas HaMinchah</i>."</span> They also warned not to begin anything close to <span class="h">Minchah</span>: <span class="mx">"one should not sit before the barber close to <i>Minchah</i> without first praying; one should not enter a bathhouse..."</span></div>

<div class="p">Based on the teaching "<span class="h">Vayomer Hashem el Moshe: Bo el Pharaoh, ki Ani hichbadti es libo</span>" (<span class="lr">LM I:64</span>). See the entire teaching there and understand well — these are exceedingly deep and wondrous matters.</div>

<div class="p">The principle: all the wisdoms, difficulties, heresies, and confusions for which there is no answer — all come from the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> [the Vacated Space], from which Hashem contracted His G-dliness, as it were, for the purpose of creating the world (without this, creation would have been impossible — everything would have been One). Since these inquiries and difficulties come from the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> (from which He contracted His G-dliness), it is certainly impossible in any manner to understand these inquiries or resolve these difficulties. For if one could understand and resolve them, one would find Hashem there as well — but in truth, one cannot find Hashem there through inquiries from the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> (He contracted His G-dliness from there for the world's creation). Therefore regarding these inquiries it is said: <span class="v">"all who enter her shall not return"</span> — it is forbidden to enter these inquiries at all, for one will certainly never understand them or find a resolution. One can only rely on <span class="h">emunah</span> alone — believing in Hashem with complete <span class="h">emunah</span> without any inquiries whatsoever.</div>

<div class="p">In absolute truth, Hashem is certainly found there too, even in the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> — certainly nothing exists without His vitality. But it is impossible to understand this in any way until the future — when the contraction of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> will be understood: how He contracted the radiance of His G-dliness from there, yet He is found there nonetheless. In this world it cannot be understood at all — one must rely solely on <span class="h">emunah</span>. (This is why Israel are called <span class="h">Ivriim</span> — because they have <span class="h">emunah</span>; see there.) Only the exceedingly great <span class="h">tzadik</span> (the aspect of Moshe) can enter there — and he must enter to raise from there all the souls that fell there. Through the song that this exceedingly great <span class="h">tzadik</span> sings, he raises them: <span class="v">"then Moshe sang"</span>; <span class="v">"you shall come, you shall gaze from the peak of <i>Amanah</i> [faith]."</span> See all this there well.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 1 — Each Day Is a New Creation; <i>Minchah</i> = the Contraction Before the Next Day</div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of <span class="h">Tefilas HaMinchah</span> — toward evening as the day turns, <span class="mx">"then harsh judgment prevails"</span> (Zohar). Every day is the aspect of the world's creation: <span class="mx">"in His goodness He renews the act of Creation every day."</span> Each day a unique creation is created — each day an aspect and measure in itself: the revelation of the days and the <span class="h">midos</span>. The essential revelation of Creation (= the days and <span class="h">midos</span>) was through the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> (= the contraction). Therefore each day, before one day departs and the next enters, there must be something like the moment of the world's creation: the contraction of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> is renewed — through which the next day is revealed as a new creation. Every night precedes the day: <span class="v">"there was evening and there was morning"</span> — the world's creation: <span class="mx">"first darkness, then light."</span> The contraction of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> is the aspect of night and darkness (= withdrawal of light). Night precedes day because the contraction must precede the creation (= the revelation of light). This is: <span class="v">"the advantage of light comes from darkness"</span> — the essential revelation of light is from the darkness (= the contraction).</div>

<div class="p">This is also the aspect of the moon's diminishment: <span class="mx">"two kings cannot share one crown"</span> — there would be no room for creation. <span class="mx">"Go and diminish yourself"</span> — the contraction of light, making room for the world's creation, governed through the moon (= <span class="h">malchus</span>).</div>

<div class="sn">§ 2 — Why There Is No <i>Krias Shma</i> at <i>Minchah</i>: Only <i>Emunah</i> Without <i>Da'as</i></div>

<div class="p">Every day, after midday, the sun begins to diminish — until midday it grows brighter, then afterward contracts and diminishes so it does not spread excessively (it must diminish for the world's creation — renewing the next day's creation, impossible without the contraction of light). The contraction is the intensification of judgment — all heresies, all difficulties of the philosophers and deniers, all come from the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>. As long as idolatry (= heresies and <span class="h">apikorsus</span>) exists in the world, <span class="h">charon af</span> is in the world. All good and <span class="h">chesed</span> is Hashem's light: <span class="v">"Hashem is good to all."</span> Whoever removes Hashem's light from himself through inquiries and difficulties — removes all good, and judgments prevail over him.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore at <span class="h">Minchah</span> time (= after midday = the contraction of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>), harsh judgment prevails. The Sages established <span class="h">Tefilas HaMinchah</span> then and warned greatly: strengthen and exert yourself to pray it with concentration, not letting its time pass. <span class="h">Tefilah</span> is the aspect of <span class="h">emunah</span>, as Rabbainu writes in many places: <span class="v">"his hands were <i>emunah</i>"</span> — the Targum translates: <span class="mx">"spread in prayer."</span> In the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>, one is forbidden to investigate with one's mind at all — only rely on <span class="h">emunah</span>. Through <span class="h">emunah</span>, one believes that even there, in the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>, He is found — though it cannot be understood by intellect at all.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore at <span class="h">Minchah</span> there is no <span class="h">Krias Shma</span> — only <span class="h">tefilah</span> alone. <span class="h">Krias Shma</span> is the drawing of <span class="h">mochin</span> [intellect], as known. At <span class="h">Minchah</span> (= the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>), one cannot enter with <span class="h">da'as</span> at all — only with <span class="h">emunah</span>. <span class="h">Krias Shma</span>, though it is <span class="h">emunah</span>, is also <span class="h">mochin</span> — the <span class="h">emunah</span> of "after Creation" (nullifying the heresies from the residue of the breaking of the vessels). There, though one also relies on <span class="h">emunah</span>, there is also <span class="h">da'as</span> — whoever merits can understand with intellect. <span class="h">Krias Shma</span> = <span class="h">emunah</span> + <span class="h">mochin</span> (after Creation, one can find Him with intellect alongside <span class="h">emunah</span>). But <span class="h">Tefilas HaMinchah</span> is the aspect of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> (= the contraction) — where one cannot enter with <span class="h">da'as</span> at all, only <span class="h">emunah</span>. <span class="h">Tefilah</span> is solely <span class="h">d'vaikus</span>, self-nullification, and <span class="h">emunah</span> — beyond nature, beyond Creation, "before Creation." (<span class="h">Tefilah</span> is creation-in-potential; Torah is creation-in-actuality.) Therefore at <span class="h">Minchah</span> we pray only <span class="h">tefilah</span> (= <span class="h">emunah</span> and <span class="h">d'vaikus</span> alone), without <span class="h">Krias Shma</span> — then is not the time for drawing <span class="h">mochin</span>.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 3 — <i>Minchah</i> Is Harsher Than the Night Itself: The Contraction Lasts Only an Instant</div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Minchah</span> time is harsher than the night itself (as brought in the <span class="h">Kavanos</span>). In truth, the essential contraction of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> (= the withdrawal of light for the world's creation) is only momentary — in the blink of an eye, at the instant of contraction alone. Immediately upon the light being contracted, the filling of the contraction with His light began — instantly the creation of the world commenced (= the revelation of the days and <span class="h">midos</span>). The essential contraction is only momentary.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore the essential contraction of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> is only at <span class="h">Minchah</span> time — as the day turns, the light contracts for the next day's creation. But immediately when night falls and the next day begins — though night is the aspect of contraction/darkness — the instant the contraction is complete, the light begins to be revealed within it (= the revelation of the next day's creation). Therefore immediately at nightfall, though it is contraction, the creation within the contraction begins to be revealed (the next day commences). Therefore we say <span class="h">Krias Shma</span> at <span class="h">Arvis</span> — beginning to draw <span class="h">mochin</span> (= the light of the <span class="h">midos</span> and days revealed within the contraction). Then <span class="h">Krias Shma</span> at bedtime, rising at midnight, studying Torah — through all this, <span class="h">malchus</span> (= the totality of Creation) is repaired. At dawn — the essential revelation of light from darkness — <span class="h">tefilah</span> in completeness, the essential drawing of <span class="h">mochin</span> through <span class="h">Krias Shma</span>.</div>

<div class="p">The essential contraction is only at the moment of contraction — at <span class="h">Minchah</span> specifically, when the day turns. This is: <span class="mx">"<i>bain hashmashos</i> [twilight] is like the blink of an eye — one enters and one departs, and it is impossible to stand upon it."</span> The <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> = <span class="h">bain hashmashos</span> — between day and day, when the contraction must occur for the next day's creation. But it is only the blink of an eye. The withdrawal of light for the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>'s contraction is only an instant — to make room for creation. Immediately the filling begins through the light of the days and <span class="h">midos</span> extending from the <span class="h">Ain Sof</span> into the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>. <span class="mx">"It is impossible to stand upon it"</span> — certainly it is impossible to stand upon this or comprehend it (the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> cannot be comprehended until the future).</div>

<div class="sn">§ 4 — <i>Kiddush HaChodesh</i>: Moshe's Difficulty = the Secret of the <i>Chalal HaPanui</i></div>

<div class="p">This is <span class="h">Kiddush HaChodesh</span> [Sanctification of the New Month], with which Moshe had difficulty. This is the filling of the moon — the moon's diminishment being the contraction: <span class="mx">"go and diminish yourself"</span> (since two kings cannot share one crown — there would be no room for creation). The instant the moon reaches its ultimate diminishment, it immediately begins to fill — the essential contraction is only the blink of an eye. Moshe had difficulty with the secret of <span class="h">Kiddush HaChodesh</span> — it is the secret of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> and the contraction, which no person can grasp except Moshe. Even he had difficulty until Hashem revealed it: <span class="mx">"this month."</span> He revealed this secret with the reddening of the sun (= twilight), as Rashi explains — <span class="mx">"He showed him the moon in its renewal at nightfall."</span> <span class="h">Kiddush HaChodesh</span> (= the moon's filling from its blemish) is the aspect of <span class="h">bain hashmashos</span> — at the ultimate diminishment and contraction, it begins to fill.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 5 — The Descent Before the Ascent: Every Holy Achievement Requires a Prior Contraction</div>

<div class="p">This is the descent that precedes the ascent — the descent being the purpose of the ascent. When a person ascends from level to level, it is a new creation: <span class="v">"you shall be renewed like an eagle in your youth"</span> — becoming literally a new being: <span class="v">"today I have begotten you"</span> (said of a person becoming a <span class="h">bar mitzvah</span> or whenever he sanctifies himself and takes upon himself greater service). Therefore, before meriting this ascent (= a new creation), there must be a descent — the purpose of the ascent. The descent is the contraction that must precede creation. This is: <span class="mx">"<i>tzadikim</i> — their beginning is suffering, their end is tranquility"</span> — the suffering comes from the contraction before creation. This is all the obstacles and delays before every <span class="h">mitzvah</span> or holy deed — since every holy act creates worlds (as known), there must be a contraction first (= the obstacles that precede the holy deed).</div>

<div class="sn">§ 6 — <i>Mashiach</i> Comes Only Through <i>Hesach HaDa'as</i></div>

<div class="p">This is: <span class="mx">"the son of David comes only through <i>hesach hada'as</i> [distraction/cessation of awareness]."</span> <span class="h">Hesach hada'as</span> is the withdrawal of light — the essential light being <span class="h">da'as</span> (as brought elsewhere). When <span class="h">Mashiach</span> comes, the renewal of the world will begin as if newly created — the essential creation as it should be will only be then. Therefore there must be a prior contraction: <span class="h">hesach hada'as</span> (= contraction = withdrawal of light). The instant they reach the ultimate contraction (= <span class="h">hesach hada'as</span>), <span class="h">Mashiach</span> will immediately come: <span class="v">"when He sees that the hand is gone and there is nothing held back or free"</span> — the ultimate contraction. Then immediately creation begins anew, and <span class="h">Mashiach</span> comes speedily in our days, <span class="h">amain</span>.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 7 — Yehoshua and Moshe Stopped the Sun: Revealing <i>Emunah</i> Within the Contraction</div>

<div class="p">This is why Yehoshua stopped the sun during the war against the seven nations. Their entire hold and overpowering comes from the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> (= the contraction). The contraction is the setting of the sun (= withdrawal of light). Yehoshua stopped the sun — revealing to the world the power of Israel: through their complete <span class="h">emunah</span>, they can reveal the light from within the contraction. Through this he subdued all the kings of the idol-worshippers (whose hold was from the heresies of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>). He sweetened the contraction, stopped the sun from setting: <span class="v">"[the sun] did not hasten to set — nearly a full day"</span> — revealing to all that <span class="v">"Hashem, He is G-d"</span> even within the contraction of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>.</div>

<div class="p">So too Moshe stopped the sun in the war against Amalek: <span class="v">"his hands were <i>emunah</i> until the sun came"</span> (as our Sages expound). Amalek was a great denier (as brought elsewhere). Moshe subdued him by revealing the strength of <span class="h">emunah</span> until he stopped the sun — revealing that even within the contraction, Hashem is found: <span class="v">"his hands were <i>emunah</i> until the sun came"</span> — specifically <span class="h">ad bo hashemesh</span> [until the sun came], revealing the strength of <span class="h">emunah</span> even at the time of the sun's setting (= <span class="h">Minchah</span> time, the essential contraction from which Amalek's <span class="h">apikorsus</span> derives). Moshe Rabbainu revealed the strength of <span class="h">emunah</span> even there — stopping the sun at the time it should have set: revealing that in the contraction (= the sun's setting), Hashem's light is found — thereby subduing Amalek (= the heresies and <span class="h">apikorsus</span> of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>).</div>

<div class="sn">§ 8 — Eliyahu at <i>Minchah</i>: Revealing <i>Emunah</i> in the <i>Chalal HaPanui</i></div>

<div class="p"><span class="mx">"One should always be careful with <i>Tefilas HaMinchah</i>, for Eliyahu was answered only at <i>Minchah</i>."</span> Eliyahu's essential achievement then was the revelation of <span class="h">emunah</span> — Israel was greatly astray after the vanity of idolatry and heresies. All this came from the <span class="h">apikorsus</span> of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>. Eliyahu wanted to nullify this and reveal <span class="h">emunah</span>. He was answered only at <span class="h">Minchah</span> — <span class="mx">"judgment is not sweetened except at its root."</span> Specifically at <span class="h">Minchah</span> (= the contraction of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>), one must exert oneself in prayer to reveal <span class="h">emunah</span>. The essential <span class="h">emunah</span> is needed there in the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> — when one merits <span class="h">emunah</span> there, all heresies and difficulties are nullified.</div>

<div class="p">Eliyahu exerted himself specifically at <span class="h">Minchah</span> to nullify all heresies and reveal <span class="h">emunah</span> — <span class="h">emunah</span> in the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>: knowing and believing that even there Hashem is found. Then all heresies are nullified. Therefore specifically at <span class="h">Minchah</span>, Eliyahu was answered — to reveal His G-dliness in the world and nullify all idolatry and heresies from the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>. He revealed the <span class="h">emunah</span>: even there in the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>, Hashem is found — <span class="mx">"there is no place devoid of Him."</span></div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"All the people saw, fell on their faces, and said: 'Hashem, He is G-d; Hashem, He is G-d.'"</span> <span class="h">Elokim</span> is the aspect of contraction and judgment — he revealed the <span class="h">emunah</span>: <span class="v">"Hashem, He is <i>Elokim</i>"</span> — the contraction is simple unity with Him, <span class="mx">"like the locust whose garment is part of itself"</span> — all is one. But this cannot be understood until the future. <span class="v">"They fell on their faces"</span> — they saw that in the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>, one needs <span class="h">nefilas apayim</span> [falling upon the face] (= withdrawal of <span class="h">da'as</span>). <span class="h">Panim</span> [face] = <span class="h">mochin</span> — in the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>, one must remove <span class="h">da'as</span> and rely on <span class="h">emunah</span> alone. In truth, even there He is found: <span class="v">"Hashem, He is <i>Elokim</i>."</span> They said it twice — to nullify the two types of heresies mentioned in the above teaching: heresies from the residue [of the breaking of the vessels] and heresies from the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>. Against both they said: <span class="v">"Hashem, He is <i>Elokim</i>; Hashem, He is <i>Elokim</i>."</span></div>

<div class="sn">§ 9 — The Extra Caution with <i>Minchah</i>: <i>Emunah</i> Amid the Contraction</div>

<div class="p">Therefore our Sages warned greatly about <span class="h">Tefilas HaMinchah</span> and forbade beginning anything before <span class="h">Minchah</span> — more than before other prayers (as brought in the <span class="h">Shulchan Aruch</span>). At <span class="h">Minchah</span> time, great exertion is needed to reveal <span class="h">emunah</span> through <span class="h">tefilah</span> (= <span class="h">emunah</span>). Since then is the contraction of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> — the source of the essential heresies and <span class="h">apikorsus</span> (the opposite of <span class="h">tefilah</span>, which is <span class="h">emunah</span>) — great exertion for <span class="h">tefilah</span> is needed. This <span class="h">Minchah</span> prayer is exceedingly precious — the essential thing being to reveal <span class="h">emunah</span> within the contraction of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>: revealing that even there His G-dliness is found — though it cannot be understood by intellect, only through <span class="h">emunah</span>: <span class="v">"Hashem, He is <i>Elokim</i>."</span></div>

<div class="sn">§ 10 — <i>Shabbos Minchah</i>: <i>Ra'ava D'Ra'avin</i> — the Will of Wills</div>

<div class="p">This is <span class="h">Minchah</span> of <span class="h">Shabbos</span> — when <span class="h">Ra'ava d'Ra'avin</span> [the Will of Wills] is found (Zohar: <span class="mx">"come and see: on weekdays at <i>Minchah</i> time..."</span>). <span class="h">Shabbos</span> is the World to Come (= the day that is entirely <span class="h">Shabbos</span>). In the World to Come (= <span class="h">Shabbos</span>), the intellect of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> will be revealed (= the aspect of weekday <span class="h">Minchah</span>). When this intellect of the contraction is revealed — all judgments in the world are nullified (they all come from this contraction). Therefore on <span class="h">Shabbos</span> at <span class="h">Minchah</span> specifically, all judgments are sweetened and <span class="h">Ra'ava d'Ra'avin</span> is found — the sparkling of the World to Come, when the intellect of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> (= <span class="h">Minchah</span>) is revealed. Judgments are sweetened at their root and the <span class="h">Ra'ava d'Ra'avin</span> is revealed. Through <span class="h">emunah</span> one merits Will (which is above wisdom, as Rabbainu writes elsewhere). Therefore on <span class="h">Shabbos</span> at <span class="h">Minchah</span> — nullifying the greatest <span class="h">apikorsus</span> (heresies from the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>) — one merits <span class="h">Ra'ava d'Ra'avin</span> — Will of Wills. This <span class="h">emunah</span> of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> (believing He is found even there) is <span class="h">Rosh Amanah</span> [the peak of faith] — the supreme <span class="h">emunah</span>. Through it one merits the supreme Will — <span class="h">Ra'ava d'Ra'avin</span>.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 11 — Moshe's Passing: <i>Shabbos Minchah</i> at the <i>Ra'ava D'Ra'avin</i></div>

<div class="p">Therefore Moshe departed on <span class="h">Shabbos</span> at <span class="h">Minchah</span> — at the <span class="h">Ra'ava d'Ra'avin</span>. Moshe merited this because even in his lifetime he achieved <span class="h">Rosh Amanah</span> — only Moshe could enter there (the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>). Therefore he merited departing at the <span class="h">Ra'ava d'Ra'avin</span> — <span class="h">Shabbos Minchah</span>. This is merited through <span class="h">Rosh Amanah</span>: subduing and shattering the heresies from the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> — through which one merits the <span class="h">Ra'ava d'Ra'avin</span>.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 12 — Keeping <i>Shabbos</i> Atones for Idolatry: <i>Rosh Amanah</i> and <i>Shir HaShirim</i></div>

<div class="p">This is: <span class="mx">"whoever keeps <i>Shabbos</i> properly — even if he worshipped idols like the generation of Enosh, he is forgiven."</span> All the idolatry of the early generations came from falling into the heresies of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> — they were very great sages who wanted to enter these inquiries with their wisdom, where it is impossible to stand through inquiry and intellect — and through this they fell into heresies. Through <span class="h">Shabbos</span> one merits <span class="h">emunah</span> (<span class="h">Shabbos</span> testifies to the renewal of Creation). <span class="h">Shabbos</span> is the World to Come, where this intellect will be revealed. Whoever keeps <span class="h">Shabbos</span> properly merits a taste of the World to Come — complete <span class="h">emunah</span>, <span class="h">Rosh Amanah</span>. This <span class="h">emunah</span> is revealed on <span class="h">Shabbos</span>.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore on <span class="h">Shabbos</span>, a song that is the head of all songs is revealed — <span class="h">Shir HaShirim</span>: <span class="v">"the Song of Songs, which is Shlomo's"</span> — of the King to Whom peace [<span class="h">shalom</span>] belongs (= <span class="h">Shabbos Shalom</span>). <span class="h">Shir HaShirim</span> (= the song that is the head of all songs) is the aspect of <span class="v">"you shall gaze from the peak of <i>Amanah</i>"</span> (from the above teaching) — through which the <span class="h">apikorsus</span> of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> is nullified. This is revealed specifically on <span class="h">Shabbos</span>. Therefore through keeping <span class="h">Shabbos</span> — even one who worshipped idols like the generation of Enosh (who fell into heresies of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>) is forgiven. Through <span class="h">Shabbos</span>, all these heresies are subdued and repaired — revealing <span class="h">Rosh Amanah</span> (= <span class="h">Shir HaShirim</span>): even there, Hashem is found. But now it cannot be understood until the future — the day that is entirely <span class="h">Shabbos</span>.</div>

<div class="p"><i>[Addendum:]</i> This is also <span class="h">Kiddush HaChodesh</span> — the moon's filling from its blemish at the moment of ultimate diminishment = <span class="h">Tefilas HaMinchah</span>: revealing <span class="h">emunah</span> (= <span class="h">tefilah</span>) at <span class="h">Minchah</span> time, within the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 13 — The Levites' Song and <i>Kiddush HaChodesh</i>: <i>Emunah</i> Through Song</div>

<div class="p">The revelation of this <span class="h">emunah</span> is through song and melody, as explained in the above teaching. This is what our Sages say in the <span class="h">Mishnah</span>: <span class="mx">"once the witnesses were delayed and the Levites erred in the song. They decreed that witnesses of the new month would not be accepted after <i>Minchah</i> time."</span> When the witnesses were delayed and <span class="h">Kiddush HaChodesh</span> was not performed properly — the Levites erred specifically in the song. The essential revelation of the <span class="h">emunah</span> of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span> (= <span class="h">Kiddush HaChodesh</span>) is through song: <span class="v">"you shall gaze from the peak of <i>Amanah</i>."</span> The Levites specifically played the victory-song — they are from the side of judgment (= <span class="h">Minchah</span> time = the contraction of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>), where song is needed to reveal <span class="h">emunah</span>. When the witnesses were delayed and <span class="h">Kiddush HaChodesh</span> was not performed properly — the Levites erred specifically in the song. They decreed: witnesses accepted only until <span class="h">Minchah</span> — the essential <span class="h">Kiddush HaChodesh</span> being in the aspect of <span class="h">Minchah</span> (= the revelation of <span class="h">emunah</span> within the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>).</div>

<div class="sn">§ 14 — <i>Erev Rosh Chodesh Minchah</i> = <i>Yom Kippur Katan</i></div>

<div class="p">This is the custom of increasing <span class="h">tefilah</span> on <span class="h">Erev Rosh Chodesh</span> at <span class="h">Minchah</span> — making a "<span class="h">Yom Kippur Katan</span>" with much prayer. Then one must merit <span class="h">Rosh Chodesh</span> (= the filling of the moon, <span class="h">Kiddush HaChodesh</span>) — merited only through <span class="h">Rosh Amanah</span>. This must be revealed specifically at <span class="h">Minchah</span> time (= the contraction of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>). Therefore much prayer is then added — to merit revealing the <span class="h">emunah</span>, through which the essential <span class="h">Kiddush HaChodesh</span> is achieved via <span class="h">Tefilas HaMinchah</span>.</div>

<div class="p">Then we confess and do <span class="h">teshuvah</span> for sins, praying for Hashem's atonement — calling it <span class="h">Yom Kippur Katan</span>. Sins are the aspect of heresies — they all come through the evil inclination, which is called <span class="mx">"a foreign god"</span> (= heresy). As Rabbainu <span class="h">zichrono livrachah</span> writes in the <span class="h">Alef-Bais</span> (<span class="h">Emunah</span>, §22): <span class="mx">"transgression introduces heresy into a person."</span> Therefore at <span class="h">Minchah</span> of <span class="h">Erev Rosh Chodesh</span>, we confess our sins and ask Hashem to atone for them — to subdue all heresies (whose root is in the contraction of the <span class="h">chalal hapanui</span>) and merit <span class="h">Rosh Amanah</span>: achieved through <span class="h">Tefilas HaMinchah</span> specifically, when it is with proper <span class="h">kavanah</span>. Through this one merits <span class="h">Rosh Chodesh</span> — <span class="h">Kiddush HaChodesh</span>, the filling of the moon.</div>

<div class="cn">✦ End of Hilchos Tefilas HaMinchah, Halachah 4 (§§ 1–14) ✦<br><i>Na Nach Nachma Nachman May'Uman</i></div>

